{"title":"1966 AHSME Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sides of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/d/2edcdc0d73ef64ec441f60a3a8dccdbd10aa61a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BAC$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> are in the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/877bc50f414ca24296fc237e1e72edc2de15a1eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2:3:4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is the angle-bisector\ndrawn to the shortest side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, dividing it into segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />.\nIf the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, then the length of the longer segment of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/7/7c71a13251a95d558d88dc72bb12460d5cf858ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)} \\ 3\\frac{1}{2} \\qquad \\text{(B)} \\ 5 \\qquad \\text{(C)} \\ 5\\frac{5}{7} \\qquad \\text{(D)} \\ 6 \\qquad \\text{(E)} \\ 7\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"368\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_Bisector_Theorem\" title=\"Angle Bisector Theorem\">Angle Bisector Theorem</a>, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/1/191445c54f9b86f214ef8f5b98c9c0fea3031870.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BA}{AD}=\\frac{BC}{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" /> which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f96ed08ad69dcb2c6d8f9b78fb134ede4cb1e3a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AD}{DC}=\\frac{BA}{BC}=\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"127\" height=\"38\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386888fb9aca8cffd478a238cc6eca1679786995.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=10=AD+DC=\\frac{7}{4}DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"242\" height=\"37\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/7/6e7bb8f1755f2385c2a6ea8068b4952c8e4c91b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC=\\frac{40}{7}=5\\frac{5}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"121\" height=\"37\" />.\nHence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/7/ef7ef72cd47d554d4b473d7e68935e75a19c0e7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"25\" height=\"24\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_AHSME\" title=\"1966 AHSME\">1966 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1966 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1966 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1966\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1966 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1966 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1966 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1966 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_AHSME_Problems/Problem_